1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,558
By the end of this video, you will know five habits that keep your payments private.

2
00:00:06,758 --> 00:00:11,913
One. Keep your ZEC shielded. If ZEC lands at your t1 address, shield it.

3
00:00:12,263 --> 00:00:21,252
Two. Do not shield an amount and then send the same amount to a transparent address soon after. That pattern is easy to spot.

4
00:00:22,753 --> 00:00:37,193
Three. Turn on Tor Protection. It sends your connection through the Tor network for extra privacy. Open Advanced Settings, tap Tor Protection, choose Enable, then tap Save changes.

5
00:00:37,543 --> 00:00:44,594
Four. Guard your recovery phrase. Keep it on paper. Anyone who asks for it is trying to scam you.

6
00:00:44,944 --> 00:00:54,240
Five. Check the address before you send. A t1 address is public. If you are not sure, use the address checker on the site.

7
00:00:55,740 --> 00:01:01,873
Test yourself with Phrase Guard on the site. Six quick questions, safe or scam.

8
00:01:03,373 --> 00:01:13,719
Need help? Go to support.zodl.com. Zodl will never ask for your recovery phrase. That is the whole path, zero to shielded.
